November 22nd 1963 is a point in history  that has arguably shaped all of modern  society it's the day when the world was  shaken and the fictional might of the  most powerful man in the world was  proven a falsehood is the day when the  President of the United States was  murdered in front of the entire world it  was considered the day television was no  longer in its adolescence due to the  tragic and shocking event being covered  live on news it all culminated when the  assassin Lee Harvey Oswald was himself  assassinated on live TV while being  transferred to a different police  station the event had an effect on the  entire world from that point on life  would never be as vivaciously serene as  it had been during the previous decade  some might say the American Dream died  that day  the assassination itself has been  subject to numerous conspiracy theories  and an absurd amount of speculation  throughout the years since that fateful  day but today we will tell you the truth  what really happened as well as who  really killed John F Kennedy  it all started when President John F  Kennedy and his wife Jacqueline made a  trip to Dallas Texas to hold a meeting  to build peace between Ralph Yarborough  and John Connally  however peace was never an option as  Kennedy was a controversial leader and  made several powerful enemies during his  tenure as the first president with the  x-gene the motorcade route was announced  four days prior giving the true assassin  of Kennedy plenty of time to plan the  attack that would play out as the  vehicles past the grassy knoll in a  parade like convoy the president's  ruthless vehicle was left helpless and  vulnerable at the time of 12:30 p.m.  what history is largely neglected to  inform us is just how many shooters were  involved and who was holding those  rifles that ended America's vision of  safety for many decades to come Lee  Harvey Oswald is one of the most notable  perpetrators of the crime but did he act  alone in a sense he was assisted by  powers far greater than one could  imagine the fatal shooting was filmed on  that day by onlooker Abraham Zapruder it  was very much oblivious that day to what  was happening mere feet behind him as  known vigilante Edward Blake fired a  shot that hit Kennedy directly in the  head causing his brain to splinter  backwards and forcing skull fragments  onto the rear of the vehicle Edward  Blake is a former covert government  operative that later served in Vietnam  but was discharged due to his violent  tendencies and erratic behavior during  missions Blake was positioned behind  Zapruder with the intention to shoot at  him at the event due to a brief  altercation they had at a bar the  previous night but on the day in  question Blake was still heavily niibori  too due to the excessive recreational  drinking that morning and missed his  shot hitting Kennedy instead by pure  mistake upon realizing this accident  Blake then lowers his rifle and begins  to pack his belongings being so  nonplussed by this experience that he  never stopped smoking his Cuban cigar a  fine piece of irony given Kennedy's  history however Edward Blake is far from  the only second shooter the second  second shooter is a man by the name of  James Buchanan bars  James was a member of the US Army  serving multiple tours in World War two  who is pronounced m.i.a before he could  be properly discharged although he was  thought to be dead it is now clear he  has ties to some sort of Soviet  sympathizing terrorist organization  Barnes was spotted on a water tower in  Irving Texas  he is photographed here readying his  rifle of an unknown calibre  he took his shot at 12:27 p.m. this was  also a fatal blow you may be wondering  just how many suspects were involved the  assassination was also subject to  multiple heroic yet ultimately futile  attempts at being prevented as stated  before Kennedy was the first  presidential elect to be born with the X  gene making him a prime target for  recruitment and collusion by the wanted  mutant terrorists Erik Lehnsherr also  known as max Eisenhart also known as  Magnus also known as the leader of the  terrorist cell the Brotherhood of  mutants also known as the Brotherhood of  Evil Mutants also known as the  Brotherhood being a sympathizer with  Kennedy's plight as a mutated American  he attempted to stop Lee Harvey Oswald's  second shot but was immediately tackled  by a Secret Service agent causing his  magnetic effect over the bullet to  behave sporadically and curving the  bullets path in an odd pattern that  would hit Kennedy and Governor John  Connally  thus resulting in the magic or bent  bullet Theory linter was placed in  protective custody until his prison  break in 1973 his current whereabouts  are unknown  flincher story is a tragic one as he was  one of the only men who attempted to do  the right thing that day and yet the  American people's mutant bias was so  strong at the time that he was  immediately believed to be one of the  assassins he was tackled to the ground  despite being about four feet away from  another of the second gunman the man  known as the ultimate Red Skull who had  fired from the grassy knoll with a  silenced pistol at Kennedy's head this  was a fatal shot the Secret Service had  seen him earlier but assumed he was  merely an American veteran with a slight  facial deformity given too  combat further sealing kennedy's demise  was the bullet fired from the fifth  floor of the Book Depository by none  other than Alex Mason former CIA  operative and Russian sleeper agent who  was carrying out his mind controlled  programming that was given to him in the  four Kuta gulag  by an inmate named victor Rezanov this  bullet slightly grazed Kennedy's upper  ear before ricocheting off the pavement  causing debris to strike The Spectator  by the name of James T tape on the cheek  this is not a fatal shot the mark from  the bullet has never been found due to  the bullet completely disintegrating  into the asphalt the weather of the next  few days along with the traffic and  street sweepers cover up the impact  turned in the crater into nothing but a  small dimple in the road the conspiracy  deepens as we investigate one of the  less famous assassins involved in the  murder the obscure Lee Harvey Oswald is  also speculated by many to have had at  least some input on the death of JFK  Oswald was an ex-marine Sharpshooter for  the US military who had known ties to  the Soviet Communist Party as well as a  burning hatred for the American  government however Oswald was not always  in control of his actions as over the  last several years leading up to that  fateful day his body was controlled at  random intervals by the quantum leap in  consciousness of dr. Samuel Beckett a  physicist whose mind would switch places  with strangers throughout history a  strange affliction yet on the day of the  assassination  Oswald's personality became more  dominant in the body of in Beckett's  forcing the otherwise kind-hearted  scientist to nearly commit the act  himself at the last minute before firing  his three shots Beckett was interrupted  by this man  James Franco the famed Hollywood actor  was researching for a college project by  traveling to the year 1963 in order to  stop Oswald's attempt on Kennedy's life  in altering the timeline Beckett's  personality was able to quantum leap  into the body of Secret Service agent  Clint Hill just before Oswald finally  took his shots Franco and his girlfriend  at the time Sadie  then began a physical altercation with  Oswald that ended with Franco  incapacitating the sniper with his own  rifle before the police were able to  apprehend him Oswald's second shot as  stated previously was nearly deflected  by Erik Lehnsherr before the Secret  Service became involved his third made  contact tam Beckett's consciousness did  not seal enter as a threat due to his  original time period remute and  Americans were more accepted 